WEBVTT

00:56.500 --> 00:58.274
♪ ♪

01:06.337 --> 01:07.207
Hi.

01:07.248 --> 01:09.676
I'm Ron MacFarlane,
Seth MacFarlane's father.

01:09.727 --> 01:11.820
And I'm here
to tell you the story

01:11.887 --> 01:14.199
of a very special Christmas
in Quahog.

01:14.250 --> 01:16.843
Kenny Rogers was supposed
to be here,

01:16.910 --> 01:18.971
but I think he's dead.

01:19.056 --> 01:21.483
Anyway, Seth came out
of my penis,

01:21.568 --> 01:23.778
and now he made this.

01:27.629 --> 01:32.419
<i>Our story begins in Quahog
just before Christmastime.</i>

01:32.487 --> 01:34.630
<i>The town was blanketed
with snow,</i>

01:34.681 --> 01:36.555
<i>the trees were being trimmed,</i>

01:36.640 --> 01:39.521
<i>and everyone was making up
their Christmas lists.</i>

01:51.747 --> 01:53.923
♪ Jessica Biel and Megan Fox ♪

01:53.990 --> 01:56.066
♪ Wearing nothing
but their socks ♪

01:56.134 --> 02:00.488
♪ Is all I really want
for Christmas this year! ♪

02:00.556 --> 02:02.680
Well, that's just not practical.

02:02.766 --> 02:04.774
♪ Spending a week in Mexico ♪

02:04.842 --> 02:07.019
♪ With some black guys
and some blow ♪

02:07.088 --> 02:10.436
♪ Is all I really want
for Christmas this year! ♪

02:10.504 --> 02:11.943
Oh, that sounds
terrific.

02:12.010 --> 02:13.249
How about you, kids?

02:13.317 --> 02:15.494
♪ I would like a pair
of skates ♪

02:15.561 --> 02:18.039
♪ Then I'd go out skating ♪

02:18.092 --> 02:20.751
♪ But I really don't know
how to skate! ♪

02:20.819 --> 02:22.091
Ha-ha!

02:22.159 --> 02:24.503
♪ I want a Lexus all in pink ♪

02:24.572 --> 02:26.798
♪ And a dad who doesn't drink ♪

02:26.882 --> 02:31.035
♪ Oh, and that reminds me--
12 kegs of beer! ♪

02:31.103 --> 02:35.490
♪ All these happy wishes
and lots of Christmas cheer is ♪

02:35.557 --> 02:38.403
♪ All I really want this year! ♪

02:38.471 --> 02:40.280
Santa's got his work
cut out for him.

02:40.348 --> 02:42.121
Oh, we ain't even
gotten started yet.

02:42.172 --> 02:44.399
♪ I want to tour
the Spanish coast ♪

02:44.467 --> 02:46.441
♪ Lunch with
Michael Landon's ghost ♪

02:46.509 --> 02:50.378
♪ Is all I really want
for Christmas this year! ♪

02:50.462 --> 02:51.600
Wait. What?

02:51.668 --> 02:52.974
Forget it.
Keep going.

02:53.042 --> 02:55.183
♪ Jennifer Garner in my bed ♪

02:55.251 --> 02:57.394
♪ Softer voices in my head ♪

02:57.446 --> 03:01.615
♪ Is all I really want
for Christmas this year! ♪

03:03.794 --> 03:05.903
♪ Yellow cake uranium ♪

03:05.970 --> 03:08.448
♪ Never mind the reason ♪

03:08.517 --> 03:11.143
♪ Also Chutes and Ladders
and a ball! ♪

03:12.736 --> 03:14.979
♪ Doesn't this seem
like too much stuff? ♪

03:15.047 --> 03:17.056
♪ Poo on you,
it's not enough! ♪

03:17.124 --> 03:21.510
♪ Buddy boy, I got your
Christmas right here ♪

03:21.579 --> 03:23.520
♪ All these happy wishes ♪

03:23.572 --> 03:25.630
♪ And lots of Christmas cheer ♪

03:25.699 --> 03:30.923
♪ Is all I really want
this year! ♪

03:30.991 --> 03:32.800
I'm just saying,
it seems a bit excessive.

03:32.868 --> 03:34.472
Oh, get off your soap box,
Brian.

03:34.540 --> 03:35.812
It's Christmas.

03:35.881 --> 03:37.269
And Christmas is
about gettin'!

03:37.354 --> 03:38.661
Everyone in town
knows that!

03:38.729 --> 03:41.172
♪ Japanese girls
with no restraint ♪

03:41.240 --> 03:43.182
♪ Just to choke me
till I faint ♪

03:43.250 --> 03:46.967
♪ Is all I really want
for Christmas this year! ♪

03:47.035 --> 03:49.779
Ooh, giggity!

03:49.848 --> 03:52.292
♪ Platinum-plated silverware ♪

03:52.360 --> 03:54.436
♪ Just one day
when kids don't stare ♪

03:54.504 --> 03:58.121
♪ Is all I really want
for Christmas this year! ♪

04:01.137 --> 04:05.255
♪ If you put a Christmas tree
in the public airport ♪

04:05.322 --> 04:07.767
♪ I will go to court
and sue your ass! ♪

04:07.835 --> 04:09.710
Happy holidays!

04:09.778 --> 04:11.887
♪ Wouldn't I love
a tinker toy ♪

04:11.956 --> 04:13.929
♪ And a little drummer boy ♪

04:13.998 --> 04:18.418
♪ He can either tap his drum
or my rear ♪

04:18.486 --> 04:22.371
♪ All these happy wishes
and lots of Christmas cheer ♪

04:22.438 --> 04:25.956
♪ Is all I really want
this year! ♪

04:29.439 --> 04:31.682
♪ I want a golden
mustache comb ♪

04:31.749 --> 04:33.589
♪ And some
spermicidal foam ♪

04:33.659 --> 04:40.558
♪ That's all I really want
for Christmas this year ♪

04:40.625 --> 04:42.534
♪ I want a brand-new
pitching wedge ♪

04:42.603 --> 04:44.543
♪ I would like
more Lemon Pledge ♪

04:44.611 --> 04:49.032
♪ That's all I really want
for Christmas this year ♪

04:51.144 --> 04:53.353
♪ I just want a wedding ring ♪

04:53.421 --> 04:55.832
♪ From someone named Jeffrey ♪

04:55.900 --> 04:59.918
♪ I just want
some colored Easter eggs ♪

04:59.985 --> 05:02.296
<i>♪ I want a Blu-Ray of The Wiz ♪</i>

05:02.363 --> 05:04.171
♪ We don't know
what Christmas is! ♪

05:04.239 --> 05:08.760
♪ We have something else
called Gishgemfloofneer! ♪

05:08.828 --> 05:12.612
♪ All these happy wishes
and lots of Christmas cheer ♪

05:12.680 --> 05:18.893
♪ Is all I really want
this year! ♪

05:24.722 --> 05:26.981
♪ ♪

05:29.996 --> 05:32.023
I am so excited
to see Santa Claus.

05:32.107 --> 05:34.149
You know what I think
is really wonderful?

05:34.200 --> 05:36.678
Of all the malls
in this great country of ours,

05:36.762 --> 05:38.136
he chooses to come here.

05:38.204 --> 05:39.442
Year after year.

05:39.510 --> 05:41.953
You know, I mean, who...
who are we? You know?

05:42.021 --> 05:44.164
I'll tell you who we are--
the lucky ones.

05:44.232 --> 05:45.404
Uh-oh.

05:48.386 --> 05:50.227
Oh, my God,
look at the line.

05:50.296 --> 05:51.867
Damn it, we're gonna
be here forever.

05:51.935 --> 05:53.844
Hey, wait, look!
There's Quagmire, way up front.

05:53.912 --> 05:55.637
We can cut in line
with him.

05:55.723 --> 05:57.696
Uh, wait, Stewie.
He doesn't like me so mu...

06:01.515 --> 06:03.122
Glenn? Glenn
Quagmire?

06:03.189 --> 06:04.829
Wha...
Wow.

06:04.898 --> 06:06.338
What... what
are you doing here?

06:06.406 --> 06:07.779
Oh, hi, Brian.

06:07.846 --> 06:09.385
Just waiting for Santa,
like everyone else.

06:09.453 --> 06:10.691
Wow, cool. Cool.

06:10.760 --> 06:13.004
Oh, man, we'll just hang
with you guys here.

06:13.071 --> 06:15.214
Who's this little guy? Huh?
Is this your nephew?

06:15.282 --> 06:17.155
Hey, buddy,
you here to see Santa?

06:17.223 --> 06:19.836
Yeah. I hope you've been
a good boy this year.

06:19.903 --> 06:21.979
That little guy is my
niece Abby, you douche.

06:22.047 --> 06:23.805
Her hair's short because of
the chemotherapy. Uh-oh.

06:23.873 --> 06:25.714
Do you know how much
talking it took

06:25.782 --> 06:28.529
to get her out of the house
because of her no-hair?

06:28.597 --> 06:30.237
Oh, gosh, I-I didn't know.

06:30.305 --> 06:31.977
I'm so... I'm so sorry.

06:32.045 --> 06:33.636
Oh, you're sorry?
For-For what?

06:33.703 --> 06:36.347
That waiting in line is
such a catastrophe for you

06:36.415 --> 06:37.890
that you'd rather
destroy the confidence

06:37.958 --> 06:39.498
of a five-year-old
cancer patient?

06:39.565 --> 06:41.908
Oh, come on.
I-I didn't know she was dying.

06:41.976 --> 06:43.249
Who said anything
about dying?!

06:43.317 --> 06:45.359
Uncle Glenn,
am I dying?

06:45.428 --> 06:46.932
No, sweetheart,
you're not dying.

06:47.001 --> 06:48.207
'Cause we're
gonna see Santa,

06:48.275 --> 06:50.116
and he's gonna bring
you a new brain.

06:50.184 --> 06:51.354
Get out of here, Brian.

06:51.421 --> 06:53.248
Just get out of here.

06:54.755 --> 06:56.261
Should have gone
into politics, Bri.

06:56.345 --> 06:58.773
Now we got to go to
the back of the line.

06:58.858 --> 07:00.331
What the hell! Why
isn't it moving?

07:00.398 --> 07:02.090
I don't know.
It's always the same thing.

07:02.174 --> 07:04.433
Some fat kid sitting
on Santa's lap taking all day.

07:04.519 --> 07:08.101
<i>Yeah, yeah. And I want
a Charles in Charge lunch box</i>

07:08.170 --> 07:10.881
and I want a Magna Doodle
and a new Uno game

07:10.950 --> 07:13.326
on a 'cause of
I lost the "Draw 2" card.

07:13.395 --> 07:14.934
And I want a pet animal

07:15.002 --> 07:16.476
that's half chinchilla
and half mink,

07:16.543 --> 07:17.883
'cause it'd be really soft,

07:17.951 --> 07:20.193
and I could call it chink,
and that's okay.

07:27.697 --> 07:29.002
Geez, doesn't the
mall close soon?

07:29.070 --> 07:30.309
We've been here forever.

07:30.377 --> 07:32.351
Would you relax?
We're right here. I'm next.

07:35.501 --> 07:37.074
Hello, Santa.

07:37.142 --> 07:39.285
Now, um,
we've got a slight problem here,

07:39.353 --> 07:42.097
because I have been
rather naughty.

07:42.167 --> 07:44.644
But you're a business man,
I'm a business man.

07:44.712 --> 07:48.395
I'm sure we can work...
something... out.

07:51.912 --> 07:53.253
Wait. What are you doing?

07:53.321 --> 07:54.792
Santa? You can't leave now!

07:54.860 --> 07:56.133
Hey, wait-wait, buddy, buddy,

07:56.184 --> 07:57.539
we've been in line
for, like, two hours.

07:57.607 --> 07:58.812
Sorry. I'm done.

07:58.881 --> 08:00.955
You want your kid
to sit on my lap,

08:01.024 --> 08:03.033
meet me at the bar
at Applebee's.

08:03.101 --> 08:04.371
Aw, that sucks.

08:04.440 --> 08:05.646
Sorry, Stewie.

08:05.714 --> 08:07.152
That son of a bitch.

08:07.221 --> 08:08.861
He just turned
his back on me.

08:08.929 --> 08:11.372
The way reality turned
its back on Gary Busey.

08:11.439 --> 08:13.684
How am I doing today,
Gary Busey?

08:13.752 --> 08:15.057
You're doing great!

08:15.125 --> 08:17.267
Good! Then I'll keep it up!

08:24.319 --> 08:26.228
Hey, give me your keys.

08:26.295 --> 08:27.685
I need your car.

08:27.753 --> 08:29.090
What? You're not
taking my car.

08:29.158 --> 08:30.999
Very well, then.
You're driving me. Let's go.

08:31.067 --> 08:32.222
Dri-Driving you where?

08:32.307 --> 08:34.282
To the North Pole
to see Santa Claus.

08:34.350 --> 08:35.790
If that beslubbering,
onion-eyed maggot-pie thinks

08:35.858 --> 08:37.733
he can just blow me off
like that,

08:37.801 --> 08:39.038
he's got another thing coming.

08:39.106 --> 08:40.447
Look, Stewie, I know
you're disappointed

08:40.515 --> 08:42.120
that you didn't
get to see Santa,

08:42.188 --> 08:44.197
but I-I'm not driving
you to the North Pole.

08:44.265 --> 08:48.117
Everyone,
Quagmire's niece is in the ICU.

08:48.184 --> 08:50.628
Now, I think we should go
down there to support him.

08:50.696 --> 08:52.336
Wh-What?
Yeah, apparently,

08:52.405 --> 08:53.676
something happened at the mall,

08:53.743 --> 08:55.618
and she took a turn
for the worse.

08:55.686 --> 08:57.697
They don't know how much time
she has left.

08:57.764 --> 08:58.867
Quagmire just called.

08:58.935 --> 09:00.375
He's really upset.

09:00.443 --> 09:02.284
It doesn't sound
like he wants us there

09:02.352 --> 09:04.361
for some reason,
but-but we should go anyway.

09:04.428 --> 09:07.008
All right, let's go
to the North Pole.

09:07.075 --> 09:12.902
And so Brian and Stewie set off
on the road to the North Pole.

09:12.971 --> 09:15.683
Hey, you want
to hear a real live-action fart

09:15.751 --> 09:18.897
instead of one
of those fake cartoony ones?

09:22.919 --> 09:24.943
We're gonna need another pair
of pants...

09:25.028 --> 09:26.869
and another chair.

09:36.533 --> 09:38.626
Hey, Stewie, wake up.

09:38.693 --> 09:40.603
We're here. We're
at the North Pole.

09:40.670 --> 09:42.410
Oh, uh. What? What? What?

09:42.479 --> 09:43.649
Uh, North Pole?

09:47.737 --> 09:49.377
North Pole! North Pole!

09:49.444 --> 09:50.684
There it is!

09:50.752 --> 09:52.660
My word, I really
must have been asleep!

09:56.145 --> 09:57.315
Ah, look at this.

09:57.384 --> 09:58.923
The tip of the Earth, Brian.

09:58.991 --> 10:00.530
Okay, let's go see Santa Claus.

10:00.599 --> 10:02.441
All right, let's go.

10:04.668 --> 10:07.129
Well, this is rather
festive, isn't it?

10:09.306 --> 10:12.037
Small.

10:14.330 --> 10:17.529
Well, it has to be small
because of all the tiny elves.

10:17.613 --> 10:18.703
Ah, that's right.

10:18.787 --> 10:19.959
Good. Good point. Elves.

10:20.027 --> 10:21.532
Yo, yo, what's up, y'alls?

10:21.600 --> 10:25.049
Y'alls ready to kick it
in some fine North Pole gear?

10:25.117 --> 10:28.868
Brian, why does the North Pole
have black teenagers?

10:28.919 --> 10:31.547
Uh... 'cause...
from, uh, Katrina?

10:31.598 --> 10:32.953
Ah, of course. All right.

10:33.022 --> 10:35.366
Well, uh, I just have
one more question, then.

10:35.432 --> 10:37.794
Do you think I'm an idiot?!
Huh? Do you?

10:37.878 --> 10:40.223
Look, Stewie, the North Pole
is a long and dangerous...

10:40.290 --> 10:43.304
You can't jerk me around when
it comes to Santa Claus, Brian!

10:43.356 --> 10:46.084
There is a Ferris wheel here,
and a guy hosing vomit!

10:46.152 --> 10:47.825
Nobody vomits
at the North Pole!

10:47.876 --> 10:51.811
Except for Santa's wife because
she has an eating disorder!

10:51.862 --> 10:54.691
What? Yeah, 'cause he can have
anyone he wants, and she knows that!

10:54.759 --> 10:56.165
Stewie, just pull
yourself together.

10:56.233 --> 10:57.706
I won't, Brian!

10:57.775 --> 10:59.765
Now you get your ass back
into that hippie car of yours

10:59.851 --> 11:01.224
and take me
to the North Pole now!

11:01.292 --> 11:02.429
Look, I know
you're upset,

11:02.498 --> 11:03.870
but why-why don't
you just sit down,

11:03.938 --> 11:05.126
write out your
Christmas list,

11:05.211 --> 11:06.966
and I promise I will
mail it to Santa Claus?

11:07.052 --> 11:08.275
Screw that.

11:08.359 --> 11:10.869
This was never about
Christmas presents, Brian.

11:10.938 --> 11:13.449
Well, then why do you want to go
all the way to the North Pole?

11:13.516 --> 11:17.602
Because... I'm going
to kill Santa Claus!

11:22.847 --> 11:26.761
<i>So it turned out Stewie was
determined to kill Santa Claus.</i>

11:27.467 --> 11:28.960
<i>Would he succeed?</i>

11:29.061 --> 11:31.220
<i>Well, let's find out.</i>

11:31.287 --> 11:33.666
Wait a minute, why the hell
do you want to kill Santa?

11:33.734 --> 11:36.043
Because that fat bastard
blew me off at the mall,

11:36.111 --> 11:37.517
and he shall not
go unpunished.

11:37.585 --> 11:39.627
Now, let's go.
I've got it all planned out.

11:39.695 --> 11:41.636
I'm gonna see the workshop,
pet a few reindeer,

11:41.705 --> 11:43.547
take a few pictures
of me and Santa,

11:43.614 --> 11:45.422
and then I'm gonna
blow his brains out,

11:45.489 --> 11:46.929
hopefully with his
bitch wife watching.

11:46.997 --> 11:49.341
This is ridiculous-- we are
not going to the North Pole.

11:49.409 --> 11:52.254
Trust me, it's a waste of time--
you're not gonna find Santa.

11:52.323 --> 11:54.398
Why not?
Because there's no such...

11:56.140 --> 11:58.686
Because when you get there,
you may find out

11:58.754 --> 12:00.595
it isn't what
you thought it was,

12:00.662 --> 12:03.106
and I wouldn't want you
to be disappointed.

12:03.175 --> 12:04.983
That's it? That's
your reason?

12:05.051 --> 12:07.798
Well, you know, you know why
nothing works out for you, Brian?

12:07.865 --> 12:09.203
Because you've got
a negative attitude.

12:09.271 --> 12:10.843
Like Eeyore.

12:10.912 --> 12:12.788
Come on, Eeyore,
let's go play.

12:12.856 --> 12:14.596
I don't feel like it.

12:14.664 --> 12:17.946
Why are you always
in such a bad mood?

12:18.013 --> 12:20.656
I have a nail in my anus.
Oh.

12:20.725 --> 12:22.500
That's not fair.
I don't think I have

12:22.569 --> 12:23.673
a negative attitude.
I just...

12:23.741 --> 12:25.616
I-I don't think
it's a good idea for us

12:25.683 --> 12:28.194
to embark on a potentially
dangerous journey whe...

12:28.262 --> 12:29.333
Stewie?

12:30.640 --> 12:32.583
Say yes to life, Brian!

12:32.651 --> 12:34.123
I'll be home for Christmas.

12:36.283 --> 12:37.858
Son of a bitch!

12:45.142 --> 12:46.850
So, what are we
hauling, good buddy?

12:46.918 --> 12:48.660
Oh, I got a
flock of birds

12:48.727 --> 12:50.601
that were too tired
to fly back north.

12:50.670 --> 12:52.846
Boy, this is the way
to do it, huh, Jerry?

12:52.913 --> 12:55.191
Sure is. Think
this makes us lazy?

12:55.259 --> 12:58.407
Nah, we're still
in the V-shape.

13:39.671 --> 13:41.915
What is this?
This is a weird gun.

13:41.983 --> 13:43.256
Yeah. Don't touch that.

13:43.323 --> 13:44.730
Oh, it's a flare gun.

13:44.797 --> 13:46.337
Maybe you should
put that back.

13:46.405 --> 13:48.363
I'm just holding it.
Is this the trigger?

14:27.604 --> 14:29.913
Oh, my God, Stewie,
you all right?

14:29.981 --> 14:31.219
What the hell
happened?

14:31.287 --> 14:33.966
Eh, just some stupid
stuff went down.

14:34.033 --> 14:35.341
You could have
been killed!

14:35.408 --> 14:36.546
I could have
been killed!

14:36.614 --> 14:37.818
Look at my car!

14:37.886 --> 14:39.793
Well, you know, if
you had just taken me

14:39.861 --> 14:41.503
<i>to the real North Pole
to see Santa,</i>

14:41.571 --> 14:43.747
none of this
would have happened!

14:43.814 --> 14:45.288
Wh-Wh-What is this?
What are you doing?

14:45.355 --> 14:46.560
Hitching a ride.

14:46.627 --> 14:48.671
I'm gonna keep heading
north until I find Santa.

14:48.738 --> 14:50.010
Stewie, you're not
gonna find him.

14:50.079 --> 14:51.384
You do what you
want, Brian,

14:51.451 --> 14:53.224
but I am going
to the North Pole

14:53.292 --> 14:54.766
and I'm gonna kill
that bastard!

14:54.835 --> 14:57.077
Stewie, you're putting me
in a hell of a position here,

14:57.145 --> 14:58.618
but I have no choice.

14:58.686 --> 15:00.059
You're not gonna
kill Santa Claus,

15:00.127 --> 15:01.499
because he doesn't exist.

15:02.772 --> 15:05.419
R-R-Really, Brian?

15:05.487 --> 15:06.891
He doesn't exist?

15:06.960 --> 15:08.399
That's right,
he's not real.

15:08.467 --> 15:10.041
Oh, interesting.
Interesting theory, Brian.

15:10.108 --> 15:11.915
Um, who else
isn't real, hmm?

15:11.983 --> 15:14.193
You gonna tell me
that Elmo isn't real?

15:14.261 --> 15:17.175
Huh? SpongeBob?
Is he not real, Brian?

15:17.242 --> 15:20.189
Is-is SpongeBob not there
at the bottom of the ocean

15:20.256 --> 15:22.199
giving Squidward
the business? Hmm?

15:22.266 --> 15:24.141
And what about
Curious George?

15:24.209 --> 15:26.786
Huh? Does he not
really exist? Hmm?

15:26.854 --> 15:28.728
Is Curious George
not really out there

15:28.797 --> 15:30.472
making little boats
out of newspapers

15:30.540 --> 15:32.481
that he should be
delivering? Huh?

15:32.549 --> 15:34.490
Educate yourself,
you fool.

15:34.558 --> 15:36.332
Look, Stewie, if you'd
just listen for a sec...

15:36.400 --> 15:37.639
No, you listen, Brian!

15:37.707 --> 15:40.454
I'll tell you what, you
take me to the North Pole,

15:40.522 --> 15:43.634
and if Santa isn't there,
I'll do something for you.

15:43.702 --> 15:45.377
What?
When Lois does that

15:45.445 --> 15:46.783
middle-of-the-night feeding

15:46.851 --> 15:49.395
where she doesn't even open
her eyes or really wake up,

15:49.463 --> 15:51.739
I'll let you take that
one for me, Brian.

15:51.808 --> 15:52.945
Are you serious?

15:53.013 --> 15:54.822
Quite.

15:54.891 --> 15:56.496
Okay, you got a deal.

15:58.742 --> 16:02.358
Damn it, it
won't turn over.

16:02.427 --> 16:05.607
Great! Not even halfway through
Canada, and we're stuck.

16:08.823 --> 16:10.063
Oh, hey there.

16:10.130 --> 16:11.804
You having some
car troubles, eh?

16:11.871 --> 16:13.948
Yeah, we're trying to get
to the North Pole.

16:14.015 --> 16:16.091
I don't suppose you're from
Triple A, are you? Who?

16:16.158 --> 16:17.898
Triple A,
you know? AAA.

16:17.967 --> 16:20.178
Oh, AA, eh?
Yeah, I just came from AA.

16:20.246 --> 16:21.650
No, not AA. AAA.

16:21.718 --> 16:23.158
Yeah, that's what
I said-- AA, eh?

16:23.226 --> 16:24.632
<i>Oh, so you are
with Triple A?</i>

16:24.701 --> 16:26.876
Oh, no, that's AAA.
I just came from AA, eh?

16:26.943 --> 16:28.451
Huh? Stewie, I think
he's just a drunk.

16:28.519 --> 16:30.192
Well, drunk or not,
can you help us?

16:30.261 --> 16:32.068
I can if you want
to join AA, eh?

16:32.136 --> 16:33.608
No, I'm already
a member of AAA.

16:33.676 --> 16:35.017
I need help
with the car.

16:35.084 --> 16:37.427
Oh, I see. Yeah, looks like
you got some water leakage.

16:37.495 --> 16:39.034
You might need
a hose, eh?

16:39.102 --> 16:40.977
Jose, Roberto, whatever-- if
you've got some Latinos up here

16:41.045 --> 16:42.484
that can fix cars,
that'd be great.

16:42.552 --> 16:44.763
No, I mean, it looks
like you need a part, eh?

16:44.831 --> 16:46.336
Well, yeah, when it's
fixed, we can celebrate,

16:46.403 --> 16:47.843
but let's deal with
first things first.

16:47.912 --> 16:50.155
Well, I can probably take
you to a gas station, eh?

16:50.223 --> 16:52.767
You have cash, eh? I don't know,
my name carries a little weight,

16:52.836 --> 16:54.441
but I don't see how
that matters here.

16:54.510 --> 16:56.653
Look, we don't have enough cash
to fix the car,

16:56.720 --> 16:59.031
and we're kind of on our way
to the North Pole.

16:59.099 --> 17:01.275
Oh, a car won't take
you there, anyway.

17:01.343 --> 17:04.424
But if you like, you can
take my snowmobile.

17:04.491 --> 17:07.001
Really? You'd just...
give it to us?

17:07.069 --> 17:09.617
Oh, sure, that's what Canadian
hospitality's all about.

17:09.684 --> 17:13.099
If you like, you can have
all my money and my leg.

17:13.166 --> 17:14.237
Okay.

17:25.777 --> 17:27.031
Why'd we take his leg?

17:27.084 --> 17:28.506
Well, we're in their
country, Brian--

17:28.574 --> 17:29.979
we have to observe
their customs.

17:30.047 --> 17:31.085
Oh! Oh, dear.

17:32.595 --> 17:33.949
Well, at least we're done

17:34.034 --> 17:36.076
<i>with the first leg
of our journey, Brian.</i>

17:36.127 --> 17:38.286
Ha!
Damn right, ha.

18:08.868 --> 18:11.379
Brian, how long do you
think we've been driving?

18:11.446 --> 18:13.223
I don't know,
I've lost track.

18:13.290 --> 18:15.465
Besides, dogs don't have
a good sense of time.

18:15.516 --> 18:17.358
Could be three hours,
could be three years,

18:17.443 --> 18:18.614
I don't know.

18:18.664 --> 18:21.091
Well, we must be
pretty far north by now.

18:21.160 --> 18:23.438
Yeah, you're right. Look--
there's the aurora borealis.

18:25.849 --> 18:28.076
Yes, and there's
the aurora boreanaz.

18:28.160 --> 18:29.550
Hi there.

18:29.635 --> 18:32.046
Things are kind of
beautiful up north, huh?

18:35.998 --> 18:37.371
Oh, no!

18:37.440 --> 18:39.179
What's the matter?
We're out of gas.

18:39.247 --> 18:42.630
Out of gas? But, Brian, it's freezing out here!
What are we gonna do?

18:42.699 --> 18:44.673
I don't know. We'd better
think of something.

18:44.741 --> 18:46.582
<i>Maybe I
can help.</i>

18:46.651 --> 18:50.701
There's an old, abandoned hunting
cabin about two miles north of here.

18:50.769 --> 18:52.478
You could spend
the night there

18:52.545 --> 18:54.922
and then resume your
journey in the morning.

18:54.991 --> 18:56.395
Thanks, David.

18:56.463 --> 18:59.342
<i>Guess there are a few stars
in the sky tonight.</i>

19:01.587 --> 19:02.693
Come on.

19:02.761 --> 19:03.865
Come on, now.

19:03.933 --> 19:06.142
Okay, we'll leave you alone.

19:54.879 --> 19:56.638
All right, this
should do for the night.

19:57.228 --> 19:59.001
Look, Stewie, now that
we have a moment,

19:59.069 --> 20:01.548
I-I think we should really try to
call Lois and tell her where we are.

20:01.640 --> 20:03.044
Oh, don't worry--
I've got that covered.

20:04.587 --> 20:06.695
Hey, Lois, would you make
an appointment for me

20:06.763 --> 20:08.337
to be neutered
in two days?

20:08.406 --> 20:10.649
Well, a-are you sure, Brian?
Yes, I'm sure.

20:10.717 --> 20:12.558
And whatever I say
in two days,

20:12.625 --> 20:15.606
do not let me convince you
that I've changed my mind.

20:15.674 --> 20:18.117
Wow, you sound pretty serious
about this, Brian.

20:18.185 --> 20:20.798
Oh, I am. In fact,
I have this document

20:20.865 --> 20:22.606
that legally
binds me to same.

20:22.673 --> 20:24.247
Have you had
it notarized?

20:24.315 --> 20:27.044
No. But a notary should
be here any minute.

20:27.129 --> 20:29.707
I received a call about
notarizing a document,

20:29.775 --> 20:32.251
but I am spending
the day with my family,

20:32.319 --> 20:33.693
so they are
here, too.

20:33.761 --> 20:35.469
This is my wife, Janice,

20:35.537 --> 20:37.543
my daughters,
Lisa and Jane,

20:37.612 --> 20:40.123
and this is Rosalyn, a friend
of our daughter Jane's.

20:40.192 --> 20:41.496
Her family life is rough,

20:41.565 --> 20:43.774
so we are kind of like
a second home.

20:43.842 --> 20:45.851
Robert!
Well, it's true.

20:45.920 --> 20:47.761
Well, thank you
for taking the time

20:47.829 --> 20:49.604
to notarize this
important document.

20:49.671 --> 20:51.511
I'm sure you
are quite busy.

20:51.579 --> 20:53.320
Yes. We only have a moment,

20:53.387 --> 20:56.869
for we are taking a bus tour
of Providence and other places.

21:03.971 --> 21:07.204
The next morning,
Stewie and Brian set out on foot

21:07.289 --> 21:08.862
for the North Pole.

21:08.914 --> 21:12.595
They were cold and tired,
but Stewie was determined

21:12.681 --> 21:16.531
to carry out his plan
to kill Santa Claus.

21:16.582 --> 21:19.413
As long as I've got
all you people watching,

21:19.464 --> 21:22.261
does anyone want
to buy some pot?

21:59.607 --> 22:00.811
My God!

22:00.879 --> 22:02.185
We made it, Brian!

22:02.252 --> 22:03.524
The North Pole!

22:03.592 --> 22:05.200
See? Boom!
Right there!

22:05.267 --> 22:06.406
I told you!

22:06.474 --> 22:07.913
This is where
Santa Claus lives!

22:07.981 --> 22:09.386
In your face!

22:09.455 --> 22:10.793
I don't believe it.

22:10.861 --> 22:12.000
It's here.

22:12.068 --> 22:13.372
Damn right,
it's here!

22:13.441 --> 22:15.148
Now, while you think
about the fact

22:15.215 --> 22:16.721
that you're never
going to enjoy

22:16.788 --> 22:18.262
a nocturnal breast-
feeding from Lois,

22:18.329 --> 22:20.641
I shall open the gate.

22:39.532 --> 22:41.574
This can't be it.

22:41.642 --> 22:43.417
This can't be
Santa's workshop.

22:43.485 --> 22:45.359
This looks like
Bridgeport, Connecticut.

22:45.428 --> 22:47.403
Oh, boy, get ready
for e letters.

22:47.470 --> 22:49.513
<i>Dear Family Guy bastards,</i>

22:49.580 --> 22:52.161
who the hell
do you think you are?

22:52.228 --> 22:54.169
I'll have you know
that Bridgeport

22:54.236 --> 22:56.882
is among the world leaders
in abandoned buildings,

22:56.950 --> 22:59.092
shattered glass,
boarded-up windows,

22:59.159 --> 23:01.973
wild dogs and gas stations
without pumps.

23:02.042 --> 23:04.820
So eat my , Jew writers.

23:10.080 --> 23:11.619
Well, whatever sort
of trick this is,

23:11.671 --> 23:13.144
I will not be deterred.

23:13.228 --> 23:16.326
I'm not leaving until
Santa Claus is dead by my hand!

23:26.358 --> 23:27.531
Oh, my God!

23:27.599 --> 23:30.242
You're...
you're Santa Claus!

23:30.310 --> 23:32.454
Yeah. Who are you?

23:32.522 --> 23:35.668
I'm Stewie Griffin,
and I'm going to kill you!

23:35.736 --> 23:38.649
Ah... thank God!

23:38.716 --> 23:40.725
What?
Do it! Please!

23:40.776 --> 23:42.502
Put me out of
my misery!

23:42.571 --> 23:44.880
<i>You... want me
to kill you?</i>

23:44.948 --> 23:46.990
Come on!
What are you waiting for?!

23:47.058 --> 23:48.496
Pull the trigger!

23:48.564 --> 23:50.959
<i>Well, there isn't
a great deal of sport in that.</i>

23:54.123 --> 23:56.100
Oh, my God,
ar-are you all right?

23:57.409 --> 23:58.579
I'm okay.

23:58.647 --> 23:59.651
I'm okay.

24:00.924 --> 24:02.632
I just need to
catch my breath.

24:02.700 --> 24:04.003
I-I don't understand.

24:04.072 --> 24:06.953
I thought you were supposed
to be jolly and happy.

24:07.021 --> 24:09.365
I used to be,
a long time ago.

24:09.433 --> 24:11.641
I made toys
for little boys and girls.

24:11.709 --> 24:13.884
I loved my work,
and they loved me.

24:13.953 --> 24:15.962
But it just got out of hand.

24:16.030 --> 24:19.043
The world's population
kept growing and growing.

24:19.111 --> 24:22.327
Kids wanted more toys,
fancier toys!

24:22.394 --> 24:24.000
We used to make
wooden choo-choos

24:24.069 --> 24:25.207
and rag dolls.

24:25.276 --> 24:27.284
You ever try to make an iPod?

24:27.352 --> 24:29.191
I've got orders
for millions of 'em!

24:29.259 --> 24:31.571
Oh, that reminds me--
I need a new version of Quicken.

24:31.639 --> 24:34.149
Look at the toxic
waste we're producing.

24:41.720 --> 24:43.762
In fact, I think the
toxins are taking

24:43.830 --> 24:45.906
even more of a toll
than the inbreeding.

24:45.974 --> 24:47.883
Inbreeding?
Take a look!

24:49.274 --> 24:52.437
I started with one family
of magic elves,

24:52.488 --> 24:56.759
and every year I needed
more and more to keep up.

24:56.811 --> 25:00.611
Now they're just a sickly race
of mutated genetic disasters.

25:00.679 --> 25:03.525
At least 60% of them
are born blind.

25:08.616 --> 25:10.156
The workload destroys them,

25:10.224 --> 25:12.434
but they don't know
anything else.

25:12.502 --> 25:15.046
It's gotten so their instincts
take over, and near the end,

25:15.115 --> 25:19.165
<i>they just walk out
into the snow and die.</i>

25:22.886 --> 25:24.559
<i>Then the reindeer eat them,</i>

25:24.628 --> 25:27.540
<i>which has turned the reindeer
into wild, feral creatures</i>

25:27.607 --> 25:29.283
<i>with a blood-lust
for elf flesh.</i>

25:33.938 --> 25:35.981
<i>I don't even pray
for them anymore.</i>

25:36.049 --> 25:37.287
<i>Seems pointless.</i>

25:37.355 --> 25:39.564
<i>What god would allow this?</i>

25:39.633 --> 25:41.909
This is in none
of the songs or poetry.

25:41.977 --> 25:43.852
It's a horror show up here!

25:43.920 --> 25:45.561
How could you
let this happen?

25:45.629 --> 25:47.503
<i>Me? I didn't do this.</i>

25:47.571 --> 25:49.178
Christmas did!

25:58.423 --> 26:01.202
♪ Each bell would peal
with a silvery zeal ♪

26:01.270 --> 26:04.301
♪ As the holiday feeling
was filling us ♪

26:04.385 --> 26:07.097
♪ But now instead
all we're feeling is dread ♪

26:07.149 --> 26:10.213
♪ Because Christmastime
is killing us! ♪

26:10.281 --> 26:13.192
♪ Each Christmas list
gets us more and more pissed ♪

26:13.260 --> 26:16.106
♪ Till the thought of existence
is chilling us ♪

26:16.174 --> 26:19.055
♪ I'll tell you what,
shove your list up your butt ♪

26:19.122 --> 26:22.371
♪ Because Christmastime
is killing us! ♪

26:22.422 --> 26:25.453
♪ But can't you see that ♪

26:25.520 --> 26:28.065
♪ What you do
is a dream come true? ♪

26:28.133 --> 26:31.279
♪ Can't you see that ♪

26:31.347 --> 26:32.804
♪ Every smile ♪

26:32.888 --> 26:34.530
♪ Makes it all
worthwhile? ♪

26:34.597 --> 26:36.521
♪ No, screw you ♪

26:36.589 --> 26:38.548
♪ It's all but through ♪

26:38.616 --> 26:40.691
♪ There's too much to do ♪

26:40.759 --> 26:42.903
♪ All those dreams ♪

26:42.971 --> 26:44.611
♪ Are nightmares ♪

26:44.679 --> 26:46.553
♪ And blank icy stares! ♪

26:46.621 --> 26:49.436
♪ ♪

26:52.853 --> 26:55.262
♪ Each little elf
used to fill up a shelf ♪

26:55.330 --> 26:58.410
♪ Making playthings
and selflessly thrilling us ♪

26:58.478 --> 27:01.258
♪ Now they're on crack,
and it feels like Iraq ♪

27:01.325 --> 27:04.591
♪ Because Christmastime
is killing us! ♪

27:04.675 --> 27:07.454
♪ Each model train
only heightens the pain ♪

27:07.523 --> 27:10.769
♪ Of a workload that's
draining and drilling us ♪

27:10.836 --> 27:13.617
♪ Fingers all bleed and look,
that guy just peed ♪

27:13.686 --> 27:16.229
♪ Because Christmastime
is killing us ♪

27:16.297 --> 27:20.952
♪ But can't you see
our point of view? ♪

27:21.020 --> 27:23.162
♪ We rely on you ♪

27:23.231 --> 27:26.914
♪ Can't you see
that Christmas cheer ♪

27:26.982 --> 27:29.326
♪ Gets us through the year? ♪

27:29.395 --> 27:33.145
♪ My whole crew
is black and blue ♪

27:33.213 --> 27:34.887
♪ Can't you take a clue? ♪

27:34.954 --> 27:40.447
♪ You may think I look great,
but I'm 28 ♪

27:46.913 --> 27:49.456
♪ Each jingle bell
is a requiem knell ♪

27:49.524 --> 27:52.706
♪ And while you think it's swell
we are toiling in Hell ♪

27:52.774 --> 28:02.619
♪ Take a look, you can tell
as a man I'm a shel-l-l-l-l-l ♪

28:02.688 --> 28:06.606
♪ Because Christmastime
is killing us! ♪

28:07.780 --> 28:09.552
♪ Killing us! ♪

28:09.621 --> 28:11.362
♪ Christmastime
is killing us! ♪

28:21.262 --> 28:23.572
So Brian and Stewie
found Santa Claus,

28:24.236 --> 28:26.478
but he sure wasn't
what they expected.

28:26.547 --> 28:29.394
It turned the increasing
demands of Christmas

28:29.461 --> 28:32.140
had all but destroyed
the poor old man.

28:32.208 --> 28:33.713
Okay, look at this.

28:33.780 --> 28:36.310
Somebody gave me a little
remote control helicopter.

28:36.395 --> 28:38.236
Pretty cool, huh?

28:39.611 --> 28:42.021
Oh, it's broken.

28:50.529 --> 28:52.974
I don't know, boys,
he's in rough shape.

28:53.042 --> 28:54.715
Doctor, you've got to
do something for him.

28:54.784 --> 28:56.055
It's Christmas Eve.

28:56.122 --> 28:57.395
Christmas is the problem.

28:57.463 --> 28:59.136
He can't keep this pace up
anymore.

28:59.204 --> 29:01.247
If he goes out tonight,
he'll die.

29:01.315 --> 29:03.523
Well, then who's gonna
deliver all the presents?

29:03.591 --> 29:05.131
We will.

29:05.199 --> 29:06.304
What?
What?

29:06.371 --> 29:08.046
Stewie, look,
you were right.

29:08.114 --> 29:09.621
Santa is real.

29:09.689 --> 29:11.094
And he needs
our help.

29:11.162 --> 29:12.501
Don't worry, Santa.

29:12.568 --> 29:14.409
We'll make sure
there's a Christmas this year.

29:14.478 --> 29:15.883
Thank you, Brian.

29:15.950 --> 29:18.060
That brings me peace
in this hour.

29:18.129 --> 29:19.401
I'll be with
Allah soon.

29:19.469 --> 29:21.209
What?

29:21.277 --> 29:23.553
Uh, ye-- he doesn't know what
he's saying, he's delirious.

29:23.620 --> 29:24.893
Look, you'd better
get moving.

29:24.961 --> 29:26.670
All right, Stewie,
let's go get the sleigh ready.

29:26.738 --> 29:28.880
Is anyone else a little freaked
out by that Allah thing?

29:28.948 --> 29:30.386
Never mind that,
let's just get going.

29:38.961 --> 29:41.609
All right, Brian.
Let's do this.

29:43.735 --> 29:46.733
Go on.

29:46.801 --> 29:48.239
Giddy-up.

29:48.306 --> 29:50.768
Come on, you dumb deer.

29:52.996 --> 29:54.234
It's not working.

29:54.302 --> 29:55.675
I think they need
to be coaxed.

29:55.743 --> 29:57.451
Santa said they
eat elf flesh.

29:57.517 --> 29:59.326
Uh, oh, oh, excuse me?

29:59.394 --> 30:00.398
Uh, sir?

30:00.466 --> 30:02.575
Mr. Elf, sir?

30:02.642 --> 30:05.522
Hello? Young man?

30:07.265 --> 30:10.479
I-- I don't think
he even knows where he is.

30:10.548 --> 30:12.221
Do-do you want
to just...

30:12.289 --> 30:13.961
Yeah, I mean, uh,
I'll just...

30:14.029 --> 30:16.610
try and do it, I guess.

30:18.820 --> 30:20.963
Hey.

30:21.031 --> 30:22.336
Hey, fella?

30:44.093 --> 30:47.189
Um... okay.

30:47.258 --> 30:48.864
Bye.

31:18.591 --> 31:20.584
Hey, Brian, look.

31:20.651 --> 31:22.359
That one reindeer
just kind of pooped

31:22.427 --> 31:24.269
in the other reindeer's face,
an-and...

31:24.320 --> 31:26.579
and the other reindeer
just kind of ate it.

31:26.647 --> 31:28.724
Isn't Christmas magical?

31:40.713 --> 31:42.069
All right,
according to this map,

31:42.088 --> 31:43.812
we're approaching the
northeast coast of the U. S.

31:43.896 --> 31:45.990
Get ready to land.

32:03.458 --> 32:05.918
All right, Bri, this
is it, our first town.

32:06.002 --> 32:07.510
I'm gonna head for that roof.

32:10.190 --> 32:12.116
Why are we tilting?

32:12.201 --> 32:14.293
Look, I've never landed one
of these things before, okay?

32:16.018 --> 32:18.160
You're coming in too fast!
Look out!

32:28.446 --> 32:30.385
All right, this is good.

32:30.453 --> 32:33.167
In and out of this house
and onto the next one.

32:33.234 --> 32:34.173
What about the reindeer?

32:36.484 --> 32:37.621
Yeah, we'll cut them down
afterwards.

32:37.689 --> 32:38.894
Now let's get down the chimney.

32:46.968 --> 32:48.340
Ow! You bitch!

32:48.407 --> 32:50.350
Okay, let's get the presents
under the tree.

32:50.417 --> 32:51.589
All right, you have 'em?

32:51.657 --> 32:53.063
I thought you had them.

32:53.130 --> 32:55.507
Oh, for the love of God,
they're still in the sleigh.

32:55.575 --> 32:56.948
Aw, crap. On the roof?

33:02.442 --> 33:05.187
No, it's...
it's in the yard.

33:11.352 --> 33:12.556
Oh, my God.

33:12.625 --> 33:14.499
Didn't you unlock
the door when we left?

33:14.567 --> 33:16.039
No, you were the
last one out!

33:16.107 --> 33:18.317
Well, how the hell
are we gonna get back inside?

33:18.385 --> 33:19.423
All right, find a rock.

33:26.624 --> 33:29.706
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!
What are you doing?

33:29.773 --> 33:30.810
I'm putting out the presents.

33:30.879 --> 33:32.050
Not like that you're not.

33:32.119 --> 33:33.590
Tall in the back,
short in the front.

33:33.658 --> 33:35.633
And show some care,
for God's sake.

33:35.701 --> 33:37.442
You know, those-those
aren't socks and underwear

33:37.511 --> 33:39.084
donated by the fire department

33:39.152 --> 33:40.374
to some battered
women's shelter.

33:40.458 --> 33:42.134
Those are Santa gifts, Brian.

33:42.201 --> 33:43.438
You know, you-you have to...

33:43.506 --> 33:44.811
Wait. What-what are you doing?

33:44.880 --> 33:47.325
Did you just eat that
whole cookie off the mantel?

33:47.393 --> 33:49.400
What? They left it out
for Santa. We're Santa.

33:49.469 --> 33:51.745
Yeah, but you're not supposed
to eat all of it.

33:51.814 --> 33:53.653
You take a bite
and a sip of milk.

33:53.720 --> 33:55.530
That's how the kids know
Santa was here!

33:55.599 --> 33:57.740
Don't yell at me.
I'm not yelling at you. I'm just...

33:57.809 --> 33:59.215
I'm telling you
how it's done.

33:59.282 --> 34:01.726
They-they need some kind of
indication that Santa was here.

34:01.795 --> 34:03.334
Oh, okay, how
about this? Look.

34:03.400 --> 34:05.612
Hey, now they know he was here.
See? Stop it!

34:05.679 --> 34:07.219
Look, I'm here giving
out free presents!

34:07.288 --> 34:09.497
All right, I'll eat the
damn cookies if I want!

34:09.565 --> 34:12.478
You know what? I might
even make a sandwich!

34:12.530 --> 34:13.817
Wait. Where are you going?

34:13.886 --> 34:15.359
I'm going into the kitchen.

34:15.410 --> 34:17.135
I'm gonna make a sandwich,
get some chips or something.

34:18.407 --> 34:21.388
Brian, knock it off!

34:21.440 --> 34:22.660
Aw, man.

34:22.728 --> 34:24.001
You jackass!

34:24.069 --> 34:25.909
Hey, who the hell
are you?

34:25.977 --> 34:28.287
Uh... hello?

34:28.355 --> 34:29.661
What are you doing in my house?

34:29.729 --> 34:33.144
We're Santa
Claus... ses.

34:33.211 --> 34:34.417
Yeah, you're Santa Claus.

34:34.485 --> 34:35.655
That's why you broke in
through the window.

34:35.723 --> 34:36.896
I'm calling the cops.

34:36.963 --> 34:38.637
No, no, no.
I-I can explain.

34:38.705 --> 34:42.488
We-we came down the chimney,
but we-we forgot the presents.

34:42.556 --> 34:44.197
It's-it's actually...

34:44.265 --> 34:47.212
It's kind of a
funny story...

34:47.280 --> 34:48.685
What the hell did you do?!

34:48.753 --> 34:50.394
He was gonna call
the cops, man!

34:50.462 --> 34:52.169
You can't call the cops
on Santa.

34:52.237 --> 34:53.509
Now help me move
this guy's body!

35:06.740 --> 35:08.446
Ugh! He's still alive.

35:08.497 --> 35:10.222
All right,
tie him up.

35:10.291 --> 35:12.064
I'm gonna make it
look like a burglary.

35:13.706 --> 35:15.046
All right, look,
let-let's just go.

35:15.113 --> 35:16.352
Right, right. We'll go.

35:16.421 --> 35:19.066
I'm gonna rewrap this bat
for, um, Johnny.

35:19.133 --> 35:21.778
Let me just clean his father's
blood and hair off it.

35:21.846 --> 35:24.223
Daddy, I want a drink of water.

35:27.908 --> 35:29.015
Hey, there.

35:29.082 --> 35:30.219
How you doing?

35:30.288 --> 35:31.457
Who are you?

35:31.526 --> 35:32.664
I'm Santa.

35:32.732 --> 35:34.240
You're Santa?!

35:34.308 --> 35:35.512
Who are you?

35:35.579 --> 35:37.453
Where's Dan?

35:39.833 --> 35:41.473
Oh, my God!

35:41.541 --> 35:42.612
Oh, crap!

35:45.126 --> 35:46.598
Quick, Stewie!
Get the bat!

35:46.649 --> 35:48.741
Help! Help!

35:49.982 --> 35:51.555
Mommy!

35:51.623 --> 35:52.861
It's okay.
It's okay.

35:52.928 --> 35:54.855
Brian, see if you can
find some duct tape.

35:54.939 --> 35:56.511
Oh, my God!
Oh, my God!

35:56.563 --> 35:58.118
Mommy!
Oh, my God!
Oh, my God!

35:58.186 --> 35:59.359
Mama!

36:01.001 --> 36:02.875
All right, let's get
this place cleaned up.

36:06.562 --> 36:08.570
All right,
that's the last of the blood.

36:08.637 --> 36:10.177
Go check on the other kid.

36:10.246 --> 36:11.418
What other kid?

36:11.486 --> 36:13.828
Johnny, the one
who's getting the bat.

36:13.897 --> 36:15.938
Stewie, there's only
one bedroom up here.

36:16.006 --> 36:17.144
What?

36:17.212 --> 36:18.651
Do you have a brother?

36:18.719 --> 36:20.560
Well, then who the
hell is John...?

36:20.628 --> 36:22.838
Oh, my God, we're
in the wrong house.

36:24.515 --> 36:25.818
Damn it, we
tripped the alarm.

36:25.887 --> 36:27.494
Brian, the cops are
coming. Let's go!

36:27.562 --> 36:28.868
What? We're just
leaving like this?

36:28.937 --> 36:30.475
What about not wanting
to ruin Christmas?!

36:30.543 --> 36:31.648
It's already ruined!

36:31.717 --> 36:33.188
This was one house.

36:33.257 --> 36:35.968
We've been here for an hour
and a half! An hour and...

36:36.036 --> 36:37.643
First of all,
we're not even Santa anymore.

36:37.712 --> 36:39.017
This has been a home invasion.

36:39.086 --> 36:40.725
But an hour and a half, Brian!

36:40.792 --> 36:42.265
It's gonna be light
in six hours,

36:42.333 --> 36:44.845
and we have to deliver
to the whole rest of the world!

36:44.912 --> 36:47.355
There's two apartment buildings
on this block alone!

36:47.424 --> 36:48.831
No wonder Santa
lost his mind.

36:48.899 --> 36:50.471
This is ridiculous!
We can't do this!

36:50.539 --> 36:52.347
Nobody can. It's inhuman!

36:52.415 --> 36:53.419
All right, come on,
let's get out of here!

36:56.032 --> 36:57.405
Aw, damn,
what about the reindeer?

36:57.473 --> 36:58.661
The hell with
the reindeer!

36:58.747 --> 36:59.950
Look, they're all eating
each other, anyway!

37:03.503 --> 37:04.707
Besides, we
don't need 'em.

37:04.775 --> 37:05.946
I made a few
modifications.

37:06.013 --> 37:07.119
Hang on.

37:22.091 --> 37:24.603
That was a disaster.

37:24.654 --> 37:25.992
I can't believe it.

37:26.076 --> 37:27.616
We were supposed
to save Christmas,

37:27.685 --> 37:29.058
and we completely blew it.

37:29.125 --> 37:31.133
We failed Santa.

37:31.184 --> 37:33.646
No. No, we didn't fail Santa.

37:33.714 --> 37:35.555
The world failed Santa.

37:35.624 --> 37:37.715
He gives and gives and gives,

37:37.800 --> 37:39.742
and everyone just takes him
for granted.

37:39.809 --> 37:42.622
Hell, I-I didn't even think
he existed until last night.

37:42.691 --> 37:44.582
Well, what are we
supposed to do now?

37:44.666 --> 37:46.374
Christmas is doomed.

37:46.442 --> 37:49.456
<i>Maybe, but there is one thing
we can do.</i>

37:49.524 --> 37:50.828
Move over.

38:18.654 --> 38:19.493
Lois!

38:19.594 --> 38:21.602
There's no presents
under the tree!

38:21.670 --> 38:22.741
What?

38:24.349 --> 38:26.058
Oh, my God.

38:26.125 --> 38:28.067
Joe, did you get
any Christmas presents?!

38:28.134 --> 38:29.809
No!
Me, neither!

38:29.876 --> 38:32.152
I got eight mediocre things.

38:32.221 --> 38:33.592
Good morning, Quahog.

38:33.660 --> 38:36.340
Our top story today--
Santa Claus skips Christmas.

38:36.408 --> 38:37.747
Hopeful citizens worldwide
woke up

38:37.814 --> 38:39.421
to disappointment this morning

38:39.489 --> 38:41.330
when they discovered no gifts
from Santa

38:41.398 --> 38:42.904
under their Christmas trees.

38:42.973 --> 38:44.679
Local officials are going
with the theory

38:44.747 --> 38:46.623
that everyone was bad this year.

38:46.690 --> 38:48.900
The investigation continues
into this mysterious...

38:48.967 --> 38:51.512
Wait! I know what happened
to Christmas!

38:51.581 --> 38:52.753
Brian?!

39:00.188 --> 39:02.498
Santa Claus!

39:02.566 --> 39:04.943
That's right!
It's Santa Claus.

39:05.011 --> 39:06.820
And you've got to
listen to me.

39:06.890 --> 39:08.897
The reason there was
no Christmas this year

39:08.964 --> 39:10.521
is that this man is sick.

39:10.606 --> 39:12.915
Very sick.
And he needs our help.

39:12.982 --> 39:16.601
He's been bludgeoned by years
of greed and avarice.

39:16.668 --> 39:18.711
The workload
of filling our Christmas lists

39:18.779 --> 39:20.251
has overwhelmed him.

39:20.319 --> 39:23.702
And at the rate he's going,
he may not make it another year.

39:23.769 --> 39:25.744
But there's a way
for us to help him.

39:25.812 --> 39:29.060
If all of us everywhere
can just cut back our demands

39:29.128 --> 39:31.674
and ask for only one
Christmas present every year,

39:31.741 --> 39:34.051
there may still be hope.

39:34.119 --> 39:37.132
I know it's in our nature
to resist sacrifice,

39:37.199 --> 39:39.576
even in hard times,
but if we don't,

39:39.646 --> 39:42.825
we may have to give up
Christmas all together.

39:45.138 --> 39:48.655
Well, folks, you heard it here
first on Channel Five News.

39:48.723 --> 39:50.564
Looks like we have a choice.

39:50.631 --> 39:53.209
One Christmas gift a year
for each one of us.

39:53.276 --> 39:55.453
Can we live with that?

39:55.521 --> 39:57.631
I can.

39:57.699 --> 39:58.837
So can I.

39:58.905 --> 40:00.042
Me, too.

40:00.110 --> 40:01.215
I can, too.

40:01.284 --> 40:02.486
I can live with that.

40:02.555 --> 40:03.793
Count me in.

40:03.861 --> 40:05.233
One is enough.

40:05.302 --> 40:06.374
Aye.

40:06.441 --> 40:07.746
I can.

40:07.813 --> 40:09.890
One gift is okay.

40:09.958 --> 40:11.263
I can live with it.

40:11.331 --> 40:13.105
Okay, just one.

40:13.173 --> 40:14.780
But if it's a gym membership,

40:14.848 --> 40:17.525
somebody's getting punched
in the face.

40:24.394 --> 40:27.172
♪ ♪

40:54.522 --> 40:57.318
♪ ♪

41:24.684 --> 41:27.463
♪ ♪

41:54.812 --> 41:57.607
♪ ♪

41:57.608 --> 42:58.608
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru